/E (WebXR / Augmented Reality \(AR\) Rendering: Integrating advanced WebXR libraries \(such as Three.js\) to allow users to view fully rendered 3D models of premium furniture directly inside their physical rooms. This will utilize the user's mobile camera via Augmented Reality entirely within the standard web browser context, further removing the need for a native app.)
