1224 0 obj
<<
/Title (The development and execution of the "Dreamspace Interior Design & Home" project successfully demonstrates the powerful synthesis of modern Progressive Web App \(PWA\) architecture paired with advanced frontend User Interface engineering. By deliberately prioritizing localized client-side rendering and aggressive Service Worker caching matrices, the application systematically solves the traditional network latency and offline limitations historically associated with image-heavy, luxury design portfolios.)
/Dest [37 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 982 0 R
/Next 1370 0 R
>>
endobj
1225 0 obj
<<
/Title (The strict adherence to a premium design system, utilizing CSS custom property variables and glassmorphism techniques, ensures the platform visually communicates the luxury standards expected of the interior design industry, all while maintaining rigorous, Lighthouse-compliant software performance metrics underneath the interface. The Dreamspace platform serves as a viable, highly performant prototype for the future of digital architectural engagement.)
/Dest [37 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 982 0 R
/Prev 1371 0 R
>>
endobj
1226 0 obj
<<
/Title (Backend Database Integration: Transitioning the currently simulated frontend authentication gateway and static data structures into a fully functional backend infrastructure utilizing MongoDB or PostgreSQL. This upgrade will allow user authentication sessions to persist securely using JSON Web Tokens \(JWT\), enabling clients to save their custom Cost Estimates and favorite portfolio imagery directly to a personalized account dashboard.)
/Dest [38 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 740 0 R
/Prev 983 0 R
/Next 1372 0 R
>>
endobj
1227 0 obj
<<
/Title (WebXR / Augmented Reality \(AR\) Rendering: Integrating advanced WebXR libraries \(such as Three.js\) to allow users to view fully rendered 3D models of premium furniture directly inside their physical rooms. This will utilize the user's mobile camera via Augmented Reality entirely within the standard web browser context, further removing the need for a native app.)
/Dest [38 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 740 0 R
/Prev 1372 0 R
/Next 984 0 R
>>
endobj
