/Title (When the cursor enters the section, the `getBoundingClientRect\(\)` method fires at 60Hz, calculating the precise X and Y coordinates of the mouse pointer relative to the section's top-left corner. These mathematical coordinates are dynamically injected directly into the DOM node as inline CSS custom variables \(`--x`, `--y`\). A CSS engine rule \(`mask-image: radial-gradient`\) intercepts these variables in real-time, rendering a transparent circle at the exact location of the user's cursor, thereby revealing the hidden texture underneath while the rest of the section remains shrouded in black.)
/Dest [32 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1632 0 R
/Prev 1702 0 R
>>
