/Title (Implementation Logic: A Vanilla JavaScript event listener is explicitly bound to the HTML5 form's `submit` event. The script utilizes the `e.preventDefault\(\)` method to forcefully halt the browser's default HTTP POST network behavior. The user interface dynamically updates to render a "loading" state, providing visual feedback to the user. A `setTimeout` functional closure subsequently delays execution for 1500 milliseconds, simulating a network handshake, before issuing the `window.location.href = '/home.html'` command to route the authenticated user to the main dashboard.)
